1
00:00:01,132 --> 00:00:03,134
GIRL: Water.

2
00:00:03,259 --> 00:00:05,178
Earth.

3
00:00:05,303 --> 00:00:07,305
Fire.

4
00:00:07,430 --> 00:00:10,016
Air.

5
00:00:10,099 --> 00:00:13,811
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:13,937 --> 00:00:18,525
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:18,608 --> 00:00:22,153
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:25,990
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

9
00:00:26,115 --> 00:00:29,494
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

10
00:00:29,619 --> 00:00:31,454
an airbender named Aang.

11
00:00:31,538 --> 00:00:33,790
And although his airbending skills
are great,

12
00:00:33,873 --> 00:00:36,543
he has a lot to learn before he's
ready to save anyone.

13
00:00:36,626 --> 00:00:37,752
AANG: Oof!

14
00:00:37,835 --> 00:00:40,505
But I believe Aang can save the world.

15
00:00:47,011 --> 00:00:48,680
MAN: Previously on Avatar...

16
00:00:48,805 --> 00:00:51,474
BOY: Fire Nation killed my parents.

17
00:00:51,558 --> 00:00:53,059
I was only eight years old.

18
00:00:53,434 --> 00:00:55,979
Hello, my name is Joo Dee.

19
00:00:56,062 --> 00:00:59,816
We found out about a solar eclipse that
will leave the Fire Nation defenseless.

20
00:00:59,899 --> 00:01:05,071
It is the strict policy of Ba Sing Se that
the war not be mentioned within the walls.

21
00:01:07,365 --> 00:01:09,450
You don't understand, they're Fire Nation!

22
00:01:09,576 --> 00:01:11,869
You have to believe me.

23
00:01:11,953 --> 00:01:14,289
There is no war within the walls.

24
00:01:14,372 --> 00:01:15,957
Here we are safe.

25
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:18,960
Here we are free.

26
00:01:19,043 --> 00:01:21,838
MAN: I understand you've been
looking for your bison.

27
00:01:21,921 --> 00:01:25,508
It would be quite a shame if you were
not able to complete your quest.

28
00:01:46,654 --> 00:01:50,074
We found a printer to make our posters.

29
00:01:50,199 --> 00:01:53,494
Hey, I thought designing the
"lost Appa" poster was my job.

30
00:01:53,578 --> 00:01:55,371
I've been working all day on my Appa.

31
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:58,458
- Sokka, the arrow is on Appa's head.
-( LAUGHING )

32
00:01:59,208 --> 00:02:00,627
This is his head.

33
00:02:01,628 --> 00:02:03,630
Why are feet coming out of it?

34
00:02:03,713 --> 00:02:05,506
Those are his horns!

35
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:07,800
I haven't seen him in a while, O.K.?

36
00:02:07,884 --> 00:02:09,927
It looks just like him to me.

37
00:02:10,011 --> 00:02:12,263
Thank you, I worked really...

38
00:02:12,347 --> 00:02:14,515
Why do you feel the need to do that?

39
00:02:14,599 --> 00:02:17,018
Let's just stick with
the professional version.

40
00:02:17,101 --> 00:02:19,103
( GROWLING )

41
00:02:19,187 --> 00:02:21,230
Come on, let's get busy!

42
00:02:38,081 --> 00:02:41,334
So you're the genius
behind this incredible brew.

43
00:02:41,459 --> 00:02:43,503
The whole city is buzzing about you!

44
00:02:43,795 --> 00:02:45,588
I hope Pao pays you well.

45
00:02:45,713 --> 00:02:48,174
Good tea is its own reward.

46
00:02:48,299 --> 00:02:51,469
But it doesn't have to be the only reward.

47
00:02:51,594 --> 00:02:54,305
How would you like to have
your own tea shop?

48
00:02:54,430 --> 00:02:56,015
My own tea shop?

49
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:57,725
This is a dream come true.

50
00:02:58,601 --> 00:03:00,353
What's going on here?

51
00:03:00,436 --> 00:03:02,230
Are you trying to poach my tea maker?

52
00:03:02,313 --> 00:03:05,983
Sorry, Pao, but that's business
for you, am I right?

53
00:03:06,067 --> 00:03:10,655
Mushi, if you stay,
I'll make you assistant manager.

54
00:03:10,738 --> 00:03:13,116
Wait, senior assistant manager.

55
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:16,035
I'll provide you with a new apartment
in the upper ring.

56
00:03:16,119 --> 00:03:20,456
The tea shop is yours to do whatever
you want, complete creative freedom.

57
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:22,625
I even get to name the shop?

58
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:24,252
Of course!

59
00:03:24,377 --> 00:03:27,505
Uh, senior executive assistant manager?

60
00:03:29,048 --> 00:03:31,968
Ooh.

61
00:03:32,093 --> 00:03:33,636
Did you hear, Nephew?

62
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:38,599
This man wants to give us our own tea shop
in the upper ring of the city.

63
00:03:38,683 --> 00:03:40,143
That's right, young man.

64
00:03:40,226 --> 00:03:43,354
Your life is about to
change for the better.

65
00:03:43,438 --> 00:03:45,815
NEPHEW: I'll try to contain my joy.

66
00:04:16,846 --> 00:04:18,848
I just finished dropping all the leaflets.

67
00:04:18,931 --> 00:04:20,975
Has anyone come in with news about Appa?

68
00:04:21,058 --> 00:04:23,686
It's only been a day, just be patient.

69
00:04:25,188 --> 00:04:26,647
( KNOCKING )

70
00:04:26,731 --> 00:04:27,940
Wow, you're right!

71
00:04:28,024 --> 00:04:29,817
Patience really pays off.

72
00:04:31,652 --> 00:04:32,653
Joo Dee?

73
00:04:32,779 --> 00:04:37,241
Hello, Aang and Katara and Sokka and Toph.

74
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:38,493
What happened to you?

75
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:40,203
Did the Dai Li throw you in jail?

76
00:04:40,286 --> 00:04:42,371
What, jail?

77
00:04:42,455 --> 00:04:43,873
Of course not.

78
00:04:43,956 --> 00:04:47,543
The Dai Li are the protectors
of our cultural heritage.

79
00:04:47,627 --> 00:04:49,796
But you disappeared
at the Earth King's party.

80
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:54,550
Oh, I simply took a short vacation to
Lake Laogai, out in the country.

81
00:04:54,675 --> 00:04:56,886
It was quite relaxing.

82
00:04:57,011 --> 00:05:01,307
But then they replaced you with some other
woman who also said her name was Joo Dee.

83
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:02,767
I'm Joo Dee.

84
00:05:02,850 --> 00:05:04,310
Why are you here?

85
00:05:04,393 --> 00:05:08,439
Dropping flyers and putting up posters
isn't permitted within the city.

86
00:05:08,523 --> 00:05:10,024
Not without proper clearance.

87
00:05:10,107 --> 00:05:12,902
We can't wait around to get
permission for everything.

88
00:05:12,985 --> 00:05:15,863
You are absolutely forbidden
by the rules of the city

89
00:05:15,947 --> 00:05:17,990
to continue putting up posters.

90
00:05:19,242 --> 00:05:22,495
We don't care about the rules
and we're not asking permission!

91
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:26,707
We're finding Appa on our own and you
should just stay out of our way!

92
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:29,252
That might come back
to bite us in the blubber.

93
00:05:29,335 --> 00:05:30,503
I don't care.

94
00:05:30,586 --> 00:05:32,922
From now on, we do
whatever it takes to find Appa.

95
00:05:33,005 --> 00:05:35,383
Yeah, let's break some rules!

96
00:05:48,145 --> 00:05:51,983
I'm very disappointed in your work with
the Avatar and his friends, Joo Dee.

97
00:05:52,066 --> 00:05:54,944
I had hoped that you would be
able to control this situation.

98
00:05:55,027 --> 00:05:58,489
I'm so sorry,
but they don't trust me anymore.

99
00:05:58,614 --> 00:06:01,617
I don't think
I can keep working like this.

100
00:06:01,701 --> 00:06:05,997
Joo Dee, the Earth King has
invited you to Lake Laogai.

101
00:06:08,833 --> 00:06:11,627
JOO DEE: I am honored
to accept his invitation.

102
00:06:13,337 --> 00:06:14,630
Good.

103
00:06:14,714 --> 00:06:17,925
Now go await further orders.

104
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:23,514
If the Avatar keeps searching
for his bison,

105
00:06:23,598 --> 00:06:27,435
it could upset the delicate balance we've
worked so hard to achieve in this city.

106
00:06:27,518 --> 00:06:29,770
It could even cost us control of
the Earth King.

107
00:06:29,979 --> 00:06:31,689
Should we take care of him?

108
00:06:31,814 --> 00:06:35,776
No, it's much too dangerous for
us to confront him directly.

109
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:39,864
Let's see if we can still handle
this... Quietly.

110
00:06:45,202 --> 00:06:48,789
So I was thinking about names
for my new tea shop.

111
00:06:48,915 --> 00:06:51,751
How 'bout the Jasmine Dragon?

112
00:06:51,876 --> 00:06:55,755
It's dramatic, poetic,
has a nice ring to it.

113
00:06:56,130 --> 00:06:58,382
The Avatar's here in Ba Sing Se.

114
00:06:58,507 --> 00:07:00,509
And he's lost his bison.

115
00:07:02,136 --> 00:07:04,889
We have a chance for a new life here.

116
00:07:05,014 --> 00:07:06,891
If you start stirring up trouble,

117
00:07:06,974 --> 00:07:10,394
we could lose all the good things that
are happening for us.

118
00:07:10,645 --> 00:07:12,688
Good things that are happening for you.

119
00:07:12,772 --> 00:07:15,024
Have you ever thought that I want
more from life

120
00:07:15,107 --> 00:07:17,401
than a nice apartment
and a job serving tea?

121
00:07:17,485 --> 00:07:21,155
There is nothing wrong with
a life of peace and prosperity.

122
00:07:21,238 --> 00:07:27,328
I suggest you think about what it is
that you want from your life, and why.

123
00:07:27,411 --> 00:07:29,163
I want my destiny.

124
00:07:29,246 --> 00:07:33,209
What that means is up to you.

125
00:07:33,334 --> 00:07:35,336
The Tea Weevil!

126
00:07:35,419 --> 00:07:36,879
No, that's stupid.

127
00:07:40,841 --> 00:07:42,885
We'll split up to cover more area.

128
00:07:42,969 --> 00:07:44,971
Toph, I guess you should
just come with me.

129
00:07:45,054 --> 00:07:48,849
Why, because you think I can't
put up posters on my own?

130
00:07:52,353 --> 00:07:54,772
TOPH: It's upside-down, isn't it?

131
00:07:54,855 --> 00:07:57,984
I'll just go with Sokka.

132
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:07,576
VOICE: Katara?

133
00:08:07,827 --> 00:08:09,453
( GASPING )

134
00:08:09,537 --> 00:08:11,706
I think I can help you.

135
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:15,418
( SCREAMING )

136
00:08:15,501 --> 00:08:17,420
Katara, I've changed!

137
00:08:19,171 --> 00:08:20,297
( SCREAMING )

138
00:08:22,091 --> 00:08:24,468
Tell it to some other girl, Jet.

139
00:08:24,593 --> 00:08:25,720
( GROWLING )

140
00:08:25,845 --> 00:08:30,224
( GRUNTING )

141
00:08:30,349 --> 00:08:33,102
I don't want to fight you,
I'm here to help.

142
00:08:39,275 --> 00:08:40,985
( GRUNTING )

143
00:08:45,364 --> 00:08:47,992
SOKKA: Katara, what is it?

144
00:08:48,075 --> 00:08:50,578
Jet's back.

145
00:08:55,458 --> 00:08:57,585
We can't trust anything Jet says.

146
00:08:57,668 --> 00:08:59,462
But we don't even know why he's here.

147
00:08:59,545 --> 00:09:00,880
I don't care why he's here.

148
00:09:00,963 --> 00:09:03,090
Whatever the reason is, it can't be good.

149
00:09:03,215 --> 00:09:05,926
I'm here to help you find Appa.

150
00:09:08,429 --> 00:09:10,556
Katara, we have to give him a chance.

151
00:09:10,681 --> 00:09:12,600
I swear, I've changed.

152
00:09:12,725 --> 00:09:15,811
I was a troubled person,
and I let my anger get out of control.

153
00:09:15,895 --> 00:09:17,688
But I don't even have the gang, now.

154
00:09:17,772 --> 00:09:19,356
I've put all that behind me.

155
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:20,441
You're lying.

156
00:09:23,402 --> 00:09:24,862
He's not lying.

157
00:09:24,945 --> 00:09:26,113
SOKKA: How can you tell?

158
00:09:26,197 --> 00:09:28,365
TOPH: I can feel his breathing
and heartbeat.

159
00:09:28,449 --> 00:09:31,077
When people lie,
there's a physical reaction.

160
00:09:31,202 --> 00:09:33,370
He's telling the truth.

161
00:09:33,496 --> 00:09:35,456
Katara, we don't have any leads.

162
00:09:35,581 --> 00:09:39,794
If Jet says he can take us to
Appa, we have to check it out.

163
00:09:39,877 --> 00:09:41,504
All right.

164
00:09:41,587 --> 00:09:44,423
But we're not letting you
out of our sight.

165
00:09:45,424 --> 00:09:48,260
This is the place I heard about.

166
00:09:49,303 --> 00:09:50,596
AANG: There's nothing here.

167
00:09:51,222 --> 00:09:52,264
If this is a trap...

168
00:09:52,348 --> 00:09:54,350
I told you, I work nearby.

169
00:09:54,433 --> 00:09:57,394
Two guys were talkin' about some
giant furry creature they had.

170
00:09:57,478 --> 00:09:58,938
I figured it must be Appa.

171
00:09:59,021 --> 00:10:00,439
TOPH: He was here!

172
00:10:05,361 --> 00:10:06,821
We missed him.

173
00:10:06,946 --> 00:10:10,032
They took that big thing yesterday.

174
00:10:10,157 --> 00:10:11,659
Shipped him out to some island.

175
00:10:11,742 --> 00:10:13,285
About time.

176
00:10:13,369 --> 00:10:18,249
I been cleaning up fur and
various, uh, leavings all day.

177
00:10:18,374 --> 00:10:20,543
What island? Where's Appa?

178
00:10:20,668 --> 00:10:26,382
Foreman said some rich royal type on
Whaletail Island bought him up,

179
00:10:26,507 --> 00:10:30,427
guess for a zoo or such, though
could be the meat'd be good.

180
00:10:31,262 --> 00:10:34,014
We've gotta get to Whaletail Island.

181
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,850
Where's Whaletail Island?

182
00:10:36,267 --> 00:10:37,268
SOKKA: Far.

183
00:10:37,393 --> 00:10:38,727
Very far.

184
00:10:39,311 --> 00:10:40,604
Here it is.

185
00:10:40,688 --> 00:10:43,274
It's near the south pole,
almost all the way back home.

186
00:10:43,357 --> 00:10:46,652
Aang, it'll take us weeks just to get to
the tip of the Earth Kingdom.

187
00:10:46,735 --> 00:10:49,363
And then we'll need to find
a boat to get to the island.

188
00:10:49,446 --> 00:10:52,992
I don't care, we have a chance to find
Appa, we have to try.

189
00:10:53,117 --> 00:10:55,703
JANITOR: Must be nice to visit an island.

190
00:10:55,828 --> 00:10:58,622
I haven't had a vacation for years.

191
00:10:58,747 --> 00:11:01,000
Don't you have some more hair to clean up?

192
00:11:01,125 --> 00:11:03,085
Shuffle on, I get ya.

193
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:05,880
No more need for Old Sweepy.

194
00:11:06,005 --> 00:11:07,173
You're right, Aang.

195
00:11:07,298 --> 00:11:09,758
Right now, our first concern
has to be finding Appa.

196
00:11:09,884 --> 00:11:11,594
We can come back when we have him.

197
00:11:11,677 --> 00:11:13,053
All right, let's get moving.

198
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,555
I'll come with you.

199
00:11:14,638 --> 00:11:15,848
We don't need your help.

200
00:11:16,182 --> 00:11:18,058
Why won't you trust me?

201
00:11:19,476 --> 00:11:21,187
Gee, I wonder.

202
00:11:21,312 --> 00:11:23,981
Was this guy your boyfriend or something?

203
00:11:24,106 --> 00:11:26,108
What, no!

204
00:11:26,192 --> 00:11:29,445
I can tell you're lying.

205
00:11:30,613 --> 00:11:34,116
SOKKA: We can take the train out to
the wall, but then we'll have to walk.

206
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,577
Don't worry, on the way back,
we'll be flying.

207
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:39,580
We're finally leaving Ba Sing Se.

208
00:11:39,663 --> 00:11:42,458
Worst city ever!

209
00:11:43,375 --> 00:11:44,501
Jet!

210
00:11:44,877 --> 00:11:47,379
I thought you said you didn't
have your gang anymore.

211
00:11:47,463 --> 00:11:48,505
I don't.

212
00:11:48,589 --> 00:11:49,632
We were so worried.

213
00:11:49,757 --> 00:11:51,675
How did you get away from the Dai Li?

214
00:11:51,759 --> 00:11:52,843
The Dai Li?

215
00:11:52,927 --> 00:11:54,762
I don't know what she's talking about.

216
00:11:54,845 --> 00:11:57,514
He got arrested by the Dai Li
a couple weeks ago.

217
00:11:57,598 --> 00:11:59,141
We saw them drag him away.

218
00:11:59,225 --> 00:12:00,726
Why would I be arrested?

219
00:12:00,809 --> 00:12:02,728
I've been living peacefully in the city.

220
00:12:02,811 --> 00:12:04,813
This doesn't make any sense.

221
00:12:04,939 --> 00:12:06,982
They're both telling the truth.

222
00:12:07,107 --> 00:12:08,234
That's impossible.

223
00:12:08,359 --> 00:12:09,944
No, it's not.

224
00:12:10,027 --> 00:12:13,697
Toph can't tell who's lying because
they both think they're telling the truth.

225
00:12:13,781 --> 00:12:15,199
Jet's been brainwashed.

226
00:12:15,324 --> 00:12:16,533
That's crazy!

227
00:12:16,659 --> 00:12:18,911
It can't be.

228
00:12:19,036 --> 00:12:20,037
Stay away from me!

229
00:12:27,878 --> 00:12:31,298
( BELL RINGING )

230
00:12:37,096 --> 00:12:38,389
BOY: Out of my way, skinny.

231
00:12:38,514 --> 00:12:40,641
Ugh.

232
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:00,786
Huh? ( GASPING )

233
00:13:00,911 --> 00:13:02,913
BOY: If you don't want to end up like him,

234
00:13:02,997 --> 00:13:04,164
you'll do what I say.

235
00:13:04,915 --> 00:13:06,792
( PURRING )

236
00:13:06,875 --> 00:13:08,961
The Dai Li must have sent Jet to
mislead us,

237
00:13:09,044 --> 00:13:11,297
and that janitor was part of their plot,
too.

238
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:13,215
I bet they have Appa here in the city.

239
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,384
Maybe he's in the same place
they took Jet.

240
00:13:15,509 --> 00:13:16,677
Where did they take you?

241
00:13:16,802 --> 00:13:19,930
Nowhere. I, I don't know
what you're talking about.

242
00:13:20,055 --> 00:13:22,558
We need to find a way
to jog his real memories.

243
00:13:23,017 --> 00:13:24,518
Maybe Katara could kiss him.

244
00:13:24,601 --> 00:13:26,186
That should bring something back.

245
00:13:26,270 --> 00:13:28,230
Maybe you should kiss him, Sokka.

246
00:13:28,355 --> 00:13:30,190
Hey, just an idea.

247
00:13:30,274 --> 00:13:31,483
A bad one.

248
00:13:32,818 --> 00:13:34,611
Ooh, wait, I got it.

249
00:13:39,116 --> 00:13:41,452
I don't think it's working. Puh!

250
00:13:41,577 --> 00:13:45,372
TOPH: Try to think of something from your
past that triggers your emotions.

251
00:13:45,497 --> 00:13:48,876
SMELLERBEE: The Fire Nation, remember what
they did to your family?

252
00:13:48,959 --> 00:13:50,586
Close your eyes.

253
00:13:50,669 --> 00:13:51,962
Picture it.

254
00:13:54,089 --> 00:13:55,132
( SCREAMING )

255
00:14:03,474 --> 00:14:05,017
No!

256
00:14:05,142 --> 00:14:06,226
It's too painful.

257
00:14:07,353 --> 00:14:09,063
Maybe this'll help.

258
00:14:32,378 --> 00:14:36,090
They took me to a headquarters
under the water, like a lake.

259
00:14:36,215 --> 00:14:38,384
Wait, remember what Joo Dee said?

260
00:14:38,509 --> 00:14:41,011
She said she went on vacation
to Lake Laogai.

261
00:14:41,095 --> 00:14:42,262
That's it!

262
00:14:42,388 --> 00:14:43,889
Lake Laogai.

263
00:14:53,607 --> 00:14:55,651
SOKKA: So where's this
secret headquarters?

264
00:14:55,734 --> 00:14:57,653
Under the water, I think.

265
00:14:57,736 --> 00:15:00,072
There's a tunnel right there,
near the shore.

266
00:15:00,155 --> 00:15:01,532
( WHISTLING )

267
00:15:13,752 --> 00:15:14,753
( PURRING )

268
00:15:25,097 --> 00:15:28,100
It's all starting to come back to me.

269
00:15:30,769 --> 00:15:32,020
MAN: "I'm Joo Dee."

270
00:15:32,146 --> 00:15:33,981
"Welcome to Ba Sing Se."

271
00:15:34,106 --> 00:15:36,066
I'm Joo Dee.

272
00:15:36,191 --> 00:15:38,277
Welcome to Ba Sing Se.

273
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:41,864
"We're so lucky to have
our walls to create order."

274
00:15:41,947 --> 00:15:44,908
We're so lucky to have
our walls to create order.

275
00:15:44,992 --> 00:15:48,203
I think there might be a cell big enough
to hold Appa up ahead.

276
00:15:49,663 --> 00:15:51,623
I think it's through here.

277
00:15:56,587 --> 00:16:00,048
Expecting someone else?

278
00:16:00,132 --> 00:16:04,011
( GROWLING )

279
00:16:10,934 --> 00:16:12,769
( GASPING )

280
00:16:15,481 --> 00:16:17,024
Now that's somethin' different.

281
00:16:17,149 --> 00:16:19,985
You have made yourselves
enemies of the state.

282
00:16:20,777 --> 00:16:24,072
Take them into custody.

283
00:16:33,665 --> 00:16:34,666
( GROWLING )

284
00:16:36,835 --> 00:16:38,629
( GRUNTING )

285
00:16:44,343 --> 00:16:45,344
( GRUNTING )

286
00:16:45,844 --> 00:16:46,845
Ah!

287
00:17:02,736 --> 00:17:04,821
Augh!

288
00:17:16,291 --> 00:17:18,794
Long Feng is escaping!

289
00:17:28,845 --> 00:17:30,055
All right, Avatar.

290
00:17:30,138 --> 00:17:31,765
You've caused me enough problems.

291
00:17:31,848 --> 00:17:33,559
This is your last chance.

292
00:17:33,642 --> 00:17:35,727
If you want your bison back.

293
00:17:36,353 --> 00:17:37,646
You do have Appa.

294
00:17:37,729 --> 00:17:38,981
Tell me where he is!

295
00:17:39,064 --> 00:17:41,066
Agree to exit the city now,

296
00:17:41,149 --> 00:17:45,904
and I'll waive all charges against you
and allow you to leave with your lost pet.

297
00:17:45,988 --> 00:17:47,739
You're in no position to bargain.

298
00:17:47,823 --> 00:17:49,199
Am I not?

299
00:17:49,408 --> 00:17:51,159
You're definitely not.

300
00:17:51,243 --> 00:17:55,247
Jet, the Earth King has
invited you to Lake Laogai.

301
00:17:56,748 --> 00:17:59,167
JET: I am honored to accept
his invitation.

302
00:18:00,043 --> 00:18:01,587
( SCREAMING )

303
00:18:03,171 --> 00:18:04,339
( SCREAMING )

304
00:18:04,423 --> 00:18:07,009
( GROWLING )

305
00:18:09,219 --> 00:18:12,180
You're mine, now.

306
00:18:15,225 --> 00:18:16,268
Uncle?

307
00:18:16,393 --> 00:18:19,104
So, the Blue Spirit.

308
00:18:19,229 --> 00:18:22,482
I wonder who could be behind that mask.

309
00:18:22,608 --> 00:18:24,359
( SIGHING ) What are you doing here?

310
00:18:24,484 --> 00:18:28,030
I was just about to ask you
the same thing.

311
00:18:28,155 --> 00:18:32,618
What do you plan to do now that
you've found the Avatar's bison?

312
00:18:32,743 --> 00:18:34,745
Keep it locked in our new apartment?

313
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:37,247
Should I go put on a pot of tea for him?

314
00:18:37,372 --> 00:18:39,458
First I have to get it out of here.

315
00:18:39,583 --> 00:18:41,084
( SHOUTING ) And then what?

316
00:18:41,209 --> 00:18:43,545
You never think these things through.

317
00:18:43,670 --> 00:18:48,467
This is exactly what happened when you
captured the Avatar at the North Pole.

318
00:18:48,592 --> 00:18:51,553
You had him,
and then you had nowhere to go!

319
00:18:51,678 --> 00:18:53,597
I would've figured something out.

320
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:54,681
No!

321
00:18:54,806 --> 00:18:58,477
If his friends hadn't found you,
you would have frozen to death!

322
00:18:58,644 --> 00:19:00,979
( GROWLING ) I know my own destiny, Uncle.

323
00:19:01,063 --> 00:19:03,065
Is it your own destiny?

324
00:19:03,190 --> 00:19:06,860
Or is it a destiny someone else
has tried to force on you?

325
00:19:07,444 --> 00:19:09,905
Stop it, uncle. I have to do this.

326
00:19:10,030 --> 00:19:12,824
I'm begging you, Prince Zuko!

327
00:19:12,908 --> 00:19:19,539
It's time for you to look inward and begin
asking yourself the big questions.

328
00:19:19,665 --> 00:19:22,501
Who are you, and what do you want?

329
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:24,753
( SCREAMING )

330
00:19:24,836 --> 00:19:29,216
( SCREAM ECHOING )

331
00:19:29,299 --> 00:19:30,634
( SCREAMING )

332
00:19:30,717 --> 00:19:33,762
Jet, it's me, Aang!

333
00:19:34,179 --> 00:19:35,931
You don't have to do this.

334
00:19:36,014 --> 00:19:38,266
I'm afraid he no longer has a choice.

335
00:19:38,642 --> 00:19:40,394
JET: ( BREATHING HEAVILY )

336
00:19:40,519 --> 00:19:44,648
Ah, ah, ah!

337
00:19:45,565 --> 00:19:48,860
( GROWLING )

338
00:19:48,944 --> 00:19:50,862
Jet, I'm your friend.

339
00:19:50,946 --> 00:19:53,198
Look inside your heart.

340
00:19:53,323 --> 00:19:55,075
Do your duty, Jet.

341
00:19:57,828 --> 00:19:59,621
He can't make you do this!

342
00:19:59,705 --> 00:20:01,665
You're a freedom fighter.

343
00:20:05,669 --> 00:20:08,463
( CHEERING )

344
00:20:11,883 --> 00:20:13,593
Do it, do it now!

345
00:20:13,719 --> 00:20:15,637
( SCREAMING )

346
00:20:26,898 --> 00:20:27,899
( GASPING )

347
00:20:32,362 --> 00:20:33,780
Foolish boy.

348
00:20:33,905 --> 00:20:37,617
You've chosen your own demise.

349
00:20:39,536 --> 00:20:40,746
I'm sorry, Aang.

350
00:20:40,871 --> 00:20:42,914
Don't be.

351
00:20:56,928 --> 00:20:58,263
This isn't good.

352
00:20:58,388 --> 00:21:01,433
You guys go and find Appa,
we'll take care of Jet.

353
00:21:01,558 --> 00:21:03,059
We're not gonna leave you.

354
00:21:03,185 --> 00:21:05,520
There's no time. Just go.

355
00:21:05,604 --> 00:21:06,813
We'll take care of him.

356
00:21:06,938 --> 00:21:09,107
He's our leader.

357
00:21:09,232 --> 00:21:10,817
Don't worry, Katara.

358
00:21:10,942 --> 00:21:12,319
I'll be fine.

359
00:21:19,367 --> 00:21:20,535
He's lying.

360
00:21:21,077 --> 00:21:22,621
( CRYING )

361
00:21:32,839 --> 00:21:34,800
AANG: Appa's gone!

362
00:21:34,925 --> 00:21:36,092
Long Feng beat us here.

363
00:21:36,218 --> 00:21:40,847
If we keep moving, maybe we can
catch up with them.

364
00:21:53,860 --> 00:21:55,695
You think we could outrun them?

365
00:21:55,779 --> 00:21:57,322
I don't think it's gonna matter.

366
00:22:06,665 --> 00:22:08,124
( PURRING )

367
00:22:08,250 --> 00:22:09,251
What is it, Momo?

368
00:22:17,926 --> 00:22:19,719
APPA: ( RUMBLING )

369
00:22:20,679 --> 00:22:21,888
Appa!

370
00:22:23,682 --> 00:22:26,560
( SCREAMING )

371
00:22:29,312 --> 00:22:32,691
( SCREAMING )

372
00:22:33,191 --> 00:22:36,027
( RUMBLING )

373
00:22:40,282 --> 00:22:41,908
( GROWLING )

374
00:22:41,992 --> 00:22:44,578
I can handle you by myself.

375
00:22:56,798 --> 00:22:58,425
SOKKA: Yeah, Appa!

376
00:22:58,508 --> 00:23:00,468
( CHEERING AND LAUGHTER )

377
00:23:00,552 --> 00:23:02,596
I missed you, buddy.

378
00:23:02,679 --> 00:23:04,472
( RUMBLING )

379
00:23:14,232 --> 00:23:15,442
( RUMBLING )

380
00:23:23,658 --> 00:23:26,995
You did the right thing, Nephew.

381
00:23:29,706 --> 00:23:31,750
Leave it behind.
